"clone_url":"https://github.com/rollup/rollup.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/rollup/rollup","homepage":"https://rollupjs.org","size":33211,"stargazers_count":26142,"watchers_count":26142,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1656,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":611,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":1656,"open_issues":611,"watchers":26142,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"<!--\r\n  ⚡️ katchow! We 💛 issues.\r\n\r\n  Please - do not - remove this template.\r\n  Please - do not - skip or remove parts of this template.\r\n  Or your issue may be closed.\r\n\r\n  👉🏽 Need help or tech support? Please don't open an issue!\r\n  Head to https://gitter.im/rollup/rollup or https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/rollupjs\r\n\r\n  ❤️ Rollup? Please consider supporting our collective:\r\n  👉 https://opencollective.com/rollup/donate\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### Feature Use Case\r\nIterators can have side-effect but in many cases, e.g. when iterating arrays, they are side-effect free. This is a follow-up for #3126. Once this is implemented, `for..of` will always be penalized, which could be improved. \r\n\r\n### Feature Proposal\r\nA sophisitcated solution could track `Symbol.iterator` and `Symbol.asyncIterator` properties and check the side-effects of their return values' next function. Such a logic should also work for spread operators and manual iteration as well as interact properly with generators. It should also be tested for side-effects when passed to a function such as `Array.from`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollup/rollup/issues